PAOFLOW examples, one folder per topic. Every folder has its own README with the
inputs, the steps and, where a reference run exists, the numbers.

Quantum ESPRESSO examples: ./qe_examples/

- example01 : Si with spd pseudopotential
- example02 : Al with spd pseudopotential
- example03 : Pt with lsda (nspin = 2)
- example04 : Fe non collinear with spin orbit - Anomalous Hall conductivity
- example05 : Pt non collinear with spin orbit - Spin Hall conductivity
- example06 : AlP with non self consistent ACBN0
- example07 : Al starting from projections with overlap matrix of the atomic orbital (prior to orthogonalization)
- example08 : 2D SnTe - Spin Hall conductivity
- example09 : Weyl point search in MoP2
- example10 : Transport in GaAs with temperature and energy dependent model for relaxation time
- example11 : Calculating Rashba-Edelstein tensor elements in left handed elemental tellurium
- example12 : Bi bilayer nanoribbon site projected band structure
- example13 : Bi bilayer Z2 calculation using Z2Pack interface : SOC from QE and ad_hoc_SOC
- example14 : Layer resolved Pt spin Hall conductivity
- example15 : Si with a norm-conserving pseudopotential, internal projections and dielectric tensor
- example16 : minimal vs standard vs extended basis presets of the internal projections
- example17 : SnTe monolayer (PAW, fully relativistic) with the minimal internal projections in the augmented spinor metric; mirror Chern number

New-style property workflows: ./new_examples/

- Driver and plotting scripts in the layout written by paoflow-gen (property workflows, ACBN0, band unfolding)

VASP examples: ./vasp_examples/

- example01 : Si
- example02 : Pt (with SOC)
- example03 : Fe (with SOC, FM)
- example04 : MnF2 (nspin=2, collinear AFM)
- example05 : Mn3Ir (with SOC, noncollinear 120 degree AFM)
- example06 : FeRh (with SOC, FM) & (nspin = 2, FM)
- example07 : CrI3 monolayer (nspin = 2, FM) & (with SOC, FM)

Electron-phonon coupling: ./elphon/

- One system folder each (system.py, qe/, phonons/, coupling/, superconductivity/, optics/,
  transport/, arpes/): Si (phonon-assisted absorption, emissivity, mobility, ARPES), Pb
  (Eliashberg function, Tc, Migdal-Eliashberg gap, resistivity, infrared optics, ARPES kink),
  MgB2 (anisotropic two-gap Migdal-Eliashberg), SiC (polar crystal: Frohlich coupling,
  quadrupoles, mobility). The same layout is written by `paoflow-gen elphon`.

Non-linear optics: ./nlo_examples/

- Shift current, injection currents and second-harmonic generation: gapped graphene
  (tight-binding model), GaAs (PAW) and monolayer GeS; REPORT.md compares with the literature.

ACBN0 examples: ./acbn0_examples/

- ACBN0 / eACBN0 Hubbard U and V in MgO, ZnO, MnO (antiferromagnetic) and others, with the
  internal projections (no projwfc.x).

Tight-binding models: ./TBmodel_examples/

- Analytical tight-binding model Hamiltonians (Kane-Mele, graphene, cubium, Slater-Koster)

Band unfolding: ./unfold_examples/

- Supercell band structures unfolded to the primitive cell (DFT-PAO and tight-binding)

Quantum transport (Landauer-Buttiker): ./transport_examples/

- example01 : Transmission through a bulk system (Al)
- example02 : Transmission through a left lead-conductor-right lead system (AlH)

Quantum oscillations: ./pyskeaf_examples/ and ./qo_analysis_examples/

- Extremal Fermi-surface orbits with pyskeaf (de Haas-van Alphen frequencies and masses) and the
  comparison of the computed frequencies with measured quantum oscillations

Plotting: ./plot_examples/

- Scripts that plot the outputs of the property workflows (bands, DOS, transport, optics, phonons)

clean_runs.py removes the outputs of every example folder.
